<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 9 May, from 328 to 1960.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/328">328 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,698 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Athanasius is elected patriarch of Alexandria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Alexandrian Council elected Athanasius to succeed Alexander as patriarch of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a>. A leading defender of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicene-christianity">Nicene Christianity</a>, he spent over 17 years in five exiles ordered by four different Roman emperors.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athanasius-of-alexandria">Athanasius of Alexandria</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1009">1009 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,017 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Melus leads a Lombard revolt in Bari against Byzantine rule</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Led by the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> Melus, an insurrection broke out in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a> against the Catepanate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, the Byzantine authority based there, and quickly spread to other cities. Byzantine rule was restored when Basil Mesardonites entered Bari in June 1011.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1310">1310 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">716 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nephon, Bishop of Cyzicus, becomes patriarch of Constantinople</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nephon, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of Cyzicus, was consecrated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecumenical-patriarch-of-constantinople">Ecumenical Patriarch of Constantinople</a>. Through his willingness to compromise, the Arsenite Schism within the Byzantine Church was healed during his patriarchate, which ended with his abdication four years later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ecumenical-patriarch-of-constantinople">Ecumenical Patriarch of Constantinople</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1386">1386 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">640 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">England and Portugal seal their alliance at Windsor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-windsor-1386">Treaty of Windsor</a> pledged perpetual friendship between the two kingdoms. The Anglo-Portuguese alliance is the oldest diplomatic alliance in the world still in force.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1671">1671 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">355 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thomas Blood tries to steal the Crown Jewels</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Disguised as a parson, Thomas Blood and his accomplices overpowered the keeper of the Jewel House and fled with the crown and orb, but were caught. Charles II surprisingly pardoned him.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1864">1864 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">162 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sniper kills Union general John Sedgwick at Spotsylvania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Moments after telling his men that Confederate sharpshooters 'couldn't hit an elephant at this distance', General Sedgwick was shot dead. He was the highest-ranking Union officer killed in the war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1926">1926 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">100 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Byrd and Bennett claim to fly over the North Pole</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Richard Byrd and Floyd Bennett flew a Fokker trimotor from Spitsbergen and reported reaching the Pole. Doubts about their speed and navigation have kept the claim in dispute.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1950">1950 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">76 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert Schuman proposes pooling Europe's coal and steel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>'s foreign minister proposed placing French and German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> under a common authority, making war between them 'materially impossible'. It led to the European Coal and Steel Community.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">Steel</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1960">1960 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">FDA says it will approve the first contraceptive pill</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The US Food and Drug Administration announced it would license Enovid for contraception. The pill gave women far greater control over fertility and transformed family life.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 9 May <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/minamoto-no-yoritomo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/minamoto-no-yoritomo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Minamoto no Yoritomo</span><span class="tp">1147–1199</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/maharana-pratap"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/maharana-pratap.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Maharana Pratap</span><span class="tp">1540–1597</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/adam-opel"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/adam-opel.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Adam Opel</span><span class="tp">1837–1895</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 9 May <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/magnus-vi-of-norway"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/magnus-vi-of-norway.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Magnus VI of Norway</span><span class="tp">1238–1280</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-bradford-governor"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-bradford-governor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Bradford (governor)</span><span class="tp">1590–1657</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nikolaus-ludwig-von-zinzendorf"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nikolaus-ludwig-von-zinzendorf.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nikolaus Ludwig von Zinzendorf</span><span class="tp">1700–1760</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/friedrich-schiller"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/friedrich-schiller.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Friedrich Schiller</span><span class="tp">1759–1805</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tenzing-norgay"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tenzing-norgay.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tenzing Norgay</span><span class="tp">1914–1986</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
